<header class="page__head">
  <p class="page__eyebrow">Open metrics</p>
  <h1>Community typing data</h1>
  <p class="page__subtitle">What people actually do on GuerillaType. Aggregated, anonymous, no PII. The charts are pulled live from <a href="/analytics/">the public Umami dashboard</a>; every event is also disclosed on <a href="/privacy/">/privacy/</a>.</p>
</header>

<div class="community-stats">

  <section class="community-stat">
    <header class="community-stat__head">
      <p class="community-stat__num">01</p>
      <h2>WPM distribution</h2>
    </header>
    <p class="community-stat__lede">How fast people type here. Each finished session contributes one bucket label (a 10-wpm-wide bin). The shape settles into a log-normal curve as more sessions accumulate — most typists land in the 40–60 wpm bracket, with a long tail above 80.</p>
    <div class="community-stat__chart" data-umami-event="wpm_bucket">
      <iframe
        src="https://cloud.umami.is/share/Go6W5bgtCW47V4Gf?event=wpm_bucket"
        title="WPM bucket distribution from GuerillaType sessions"
        loading="lazy"
        referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
        allow="clipboard-write"></iframe>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="community-stat">
    <header class="community-stat__head">
      <p class="community-stat__num">02</p>
      <h2>Accuracy distribution</h2>
    </header>
    <p class="community-stat__lede">How accurate people type. Buckets cluster tight around 92–96% in published research; we expect the same here once enough sessions land. Near-perfect (99–100%) is always rare — people type fast enough to make some mistakes but not so carelessly the text breaks.</p>
    <div class="community-stat__chart" data-umami-event="acc_bucket">
      <iframe
        src="https://cloud.umami.is/share/Go6W5bgtCW47V4Gf?event=acc_bucket"
        title="Accuracy bucket distribution from GuerillaType sessions"
        loading="lazy"
        referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
        allow="clipboard-write"></iframe>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="community-stat">
    <header class="community-stat__head">
      <p class="community-stat__num">03</p>
      <h2>Mode popularity</h2>
    </header>
    <p class="community-stat__lede">Which modes do people actually finish? Time / words / quote / tape / zen / adaptive / book / lesson / drill / challenge / custom / idiom / poem — each finished session emits its mode. The relative counts tell us where to invest design effort and which surfaces serve real practice habits.</p>
    <div class="community-stat__chart" data-umami-event="mode_completed">
      <iframe
        src="https://cloud.umami.is/share/Go6W5bgtCW47V4Gf?event=mode_completed"
        title="Mode popularity distribution from GuerillaType sessions"
        loading="lazy"
        referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
        allow="clipboard-write"></iframe>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="community-stat">
    <header class="community-stat__head">
      <p class="community-stat__num">04</p>
      <h2>Speed milestones</h2>
    </header>
    <p class="community-stat__lede">Counts of sessions that crossed a milestone wpm threshold. The 50 / 75 / 100 / 125 / 150 wpm tiers each fire once per session that hits them, so the chart reads as "how many sessions cleared 80 wpm at least once."</p>
    <div class="community-stat__chart" data-umami-event="speed_milestone">
      <iframe
        src="https://cloud.umami.is/share/Go6W5bgtCW47V4Gf?event=speed_milestone"
        title="Speed milestone tier counts"
        loading="lazy"
        referrerpolicy="no-referrer-when-downgrade"
        allow="clipboard-write"></iframe>
    </div>
  </section>

