</div>

<section class="prose community-stats__methodology">
  <h2>Methodology + disclaimers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Source</strong> — anonymized event data from Umami, fired by the GuerillaType practice surface at session finish. No accounts, no cookies, no IP retained.</li>
    <li><strong>Sample</strong> — every visitor who completes at least one session contributes. There's no filter for outliers in this view; the operator's <a href="/analytics/">dashboard</a> can apply ones.</li>
    <li><strong>Bucketing</strong> — wpm and accuracy are bucketed client-side at session finish (see <code>src/assets/js/analytics.js</code>). Umami stores the bucket label as a categorical property.</li>
    <li><strong>What this can't show</strong> — per-user histories (no cookies), continuous distributions (everything's bucketed), or cross-event correlations (Umami has no JOIN). For inspiration, see TypeLit's <a href="https://www.typelit.io/state-of-typing" rel="noopener" target="_blank">State of Typing</a>; we'd love to publish similar deep cuts but the privacy posture limits what's possible.</li>
    <li><strong>Full transparency</strong> — every tracked event is listed on <a href="/privacy/">/privacy/</a>. The operator dashboard is public: <a href="/analytics/">/analytics/</a>. No event includes anything the user typed.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
